-- #2103 (FFI lib pattern rejected by the Prefix delimiter guard): a BARE
-- library name is now accepted.  Before this, `<FFI "libcurl">` was rejected
-- with *pattern "libcurl" must end in '*' or contain a '/' delimiter* — a
-- guard written for HOST/PATH prefixes ("example.com" would silently admit
-- "example.com.evil.net") and meaningless for a library name.
--
-- WHAT THE PARAM STILL VALIDATES after the carve-out: only that the string is
-- NON-EMPTY (see ffi_libname_empty_reject.mdk).  Nothing checks that the
-- library exists, and nothing cross-checks it against the `[foreign-libraries]`
-- manifest section — those are two independent facts by design (sprint Q3).
--
-- WHAT BARE vs WILDCARD MEAN: the same thing.  Prefix subsumption compares
-- `prefixConcrete` values and `prefixConcrete` STRIPS a trailing `*`, so
-- `<FFI "libcurl">` and `<FFI "libcurl*">` are one and the same set — every
-- library name beginning with "libcurl".  See ffi_libname_wildcard_accept.mdk.
extern callLib : String -> <FFI "libcurl"> Int

caller : Unit -> <FFI "libcurl"> Int
caller _ = callLib "GET /"

main : <IO> Unit
main = println "ffi bare library name accept"
